5.1 Microsoft 365

Microsoft 365 is a cloud-based subscription platform providing productivity, communication, collaboration, and security services.

Common services include:

Outlook
Exchange Online
Microsoft Teams
OneDrive
SharePoint
Word
Excel
PowerPoint
5.2 Exchange Online

Exchange Online is Microsoft's cloud-hosted email and calendaring service.

It provides:

Mailboxes
Email
Calendars
Contacts
Email delivery
5.3 Outlook vs Exchange Online
Outlook

Outlook is the client/application used by users to access email, calendar, contacts, and mailbox features.

Exchange Online

Exchange Online is the cloud email service that hosts mailboxes and provides email and calendaring functionality.

Memory
Outlook
↓
Client

Exchange Online
↓
Cloud Email Service
5.4 Shared Mailbox

A shared mailbox is a common mailbox that multiple authorized users can access.

Example:

support@company.com
        ↓
IT Support Team

Common permissions include:

Full Access
Send As
Send on Behalf
Help Desk Example

User can open a shared mailbox but cannot send email from it.

Possible area to investigate:

Send As permission
Send on Behalf permission
5.5 OneDrive

OneDrive for Business is Microsoft's cloud storage and synchronization service for a user's work files.

Common uses:

File storage
Synchronization
Sharing
File recovery/versioning features
Memory
OneDrive
↓
My work files
